          "g": 0.0,
          "i": 1.0
        },
        "species": 39,
        "text": "If you are a bold jumping spider, each of the eyes beside your two big front eyes sees an area about 70 degrees wide and about 100 degrees tall, so it reaches farther up and down than side to side. For other jumping spiders, nobody has measured these fields. Nobody has measured how far all your eyes together see around you, or how much the fields of your two side eyes overlap.",
        "cites": [
          {
            "id": "jumper#115",
