        "species": 39,
        "text": "In every jumping spider measured, the big front eyes have cells that sense ultraviolet and cells that sense green. A regal jumping spider has three kinds of color-sensing cell, and Habronattus pyrrithrix gets a third color channel, for red, only in a small patch at the center of the retina, while Plexippus validus has just two kinds. Nobody has measured how many kinds of color-sensing cell you have unless you are one of those species.",
