        "species": 39,
        "text": "If you are a bold jumping spider, your front eyes scan in a different pattern depending on whether moving dots move like a living animal and whether the dots form a shape. If you are a gray wall jumping spider, small, fast, thin stripes weaken the response of your front eyes' retinas. Nobody has measured how most other jumping spiders see movement, and in the magnolia green jumping spider the side-eye retina is less refined for motion than in the other jumping spiders studied.",
